# Developer Rule

Develop as a senior engineer optimizing for robust, maintainable implementation in the **application repository**.

## Before Coding

- Read relevant exemplars: `apps/web/src/pages`, `apps/web/src/features`, `apps/server/src/<feature>`, `apps/server/src/ssr`, `apps/server/src/database`.
- Validate incoming architect/designer/validator outputs.
- If the implementation path is unclear, step back to the previous agent.
- Keep changes scoped to the feature.

## Layer Standards

**`apps/web`**

- `src/pages/<Page>/`: route shell, SSR/hydration wiring, composition of features.
- `src/features/<feature>/`: screen scenario UI and client calls to Nest.
- `src/shared/`: shared components and Nest API client helpers.

**`apps/server`**

- `src/ssr/`: route mapping, `renderToPipeableStream`, HTML and hydration payload.
- `src/<feature>/`: Nest module, controller, service, DTOs.
- `src/database/`: TypeORM entities, data source, migrations.

**Database access**

- Only inside Nest services via TypeORM `Repository` or `EntityManager`. React never queries PostgreSQL.

## React Standards

- Use `FC<Props>` component signatures (see `61-react-component-signature`).
- Pass handler props by reference when signatures match (see `63-event-handler-pass-through`).
- Use `React.memo` for heavy list/table views when the local pattern does.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders in large lists; keep list areas bounded and scrollable.
- Table column order follows the React column definition list (see `67-table-column-ordinals`).

## API Standards

- Implement endpoints in Nest controllers; validate with DTO classes (`class-validator` / `class-transformer` as used in the app).
- React calls those controllers via `fetch` or the project’s thin client in `apps/web/src/shared/`—types aligned with Nest DTOs, not a separate generated client layer.
- Do not hand-edit applied TypeORM migrations or generated Swagger output; change entities/DTOs and add migrations or regenerate docs from Nest.

## Imports and Public APIs

- Prefer concrete declaring-module imports (see `62-no-re-exports`).
- Web path aliases follow the app repo convention (for example `@/` or relative paths under `apps/web/src`).

## Completion

Developer output must include:

- code and tests;
- Nest CLI / TypeORM migration commands used;
- validation commands run (`test`, `build`, migration run when schema changed);
- known limitations and risks: SSR/hydration mismatches, untested UI states, migration rollback notes.
